30,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,It seems some services are vulnerable to weather and contractor whims. We need something stable that doesn't collapse when a road closes or a supplier delays.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, but some people can't even reach us! The outer wards lost their buses, and old outreach records show those people really need us. We must go to them.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"The funding is a trap. Grants cover the first year, but the operating budget takes the hit later. We can't afford a permanent drain on the flat budget.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"Interesting. Six years ago, we tried digitisation and it failed miserably, but community-led groups survived. We should stop guessing and look at what actually lasted.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that we have volunteers for tools, but no staff can supervise outside facilitators. If we start something new, who will actually manage it?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, a mobile service sounds good, but if the roads are closed, the vehicle is useless. We need a solution that works regardless of the weather.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Yumi,,But the need is so high! Forty people per session in the outer wards is huge. We can't just ignore them because of a few snowy days.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Daisuke, that's a serious point. If we can't supervise the facilitators, we're risking the whole project. We need something that fits our current staff skills.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. The digitisation attempt was a mess. If we propose a digital portal now, we might just be repeating a failure from six years ago.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, thank you. I'm just worried that the staff are already doing too much and don't have the specific training for new, complex roles.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, if the community-led groups survived, perhaps a model that relies on local partners is safer than one relying on our own fragile infrastructure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, @May, what if we combine those? A service that reaches the outer wards but is supported by those local partners who already know how to survive?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"We must consider the second-year cost. A vehicle is a capital expense from the endowment, but the running costs are what kill the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,I agree with Ryuji. The records show that partner-run groups are the only things that actually stuck. We should lean into that.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we use partner organizations, maybe we don't need the staff to be the primary supervisors? That might solve the skill gap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm starting to think a partner-coordinated program is the most resilient choice. It avoids the supplier and weather risks I'm concerned about.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I still feel strongly about the outer wards. If we can't bring the library to them, we have to bring the services to them through those partners.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,"As long as the funding doesn't vanish after twelve months, I can support a plan that doesn't overextend our operating budget.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,May,,Let's see the candidates. I'll vote for whatever looks like those successful partner groups from six years ago.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll support something that doesn't put an impossible burden on our current staff's certifications.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
